# Competency: the deliberate-non-assertion report — every intentional boundary the
# ontology commits to must be enumerable, not merely respected in passing. A
# deliberate non-assertion is a logic:FormalizationCandidate typed either
# logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation (a conclusion the foundation must never draw,
# carried by a standing logic:NonEntailmentObligation and enforced by the Arm A / Arm B
# discharge check) or logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap (a mereological sharing fact
# deliberately admitted rather than disjointness-forbidden). Each row is one boundary;
# its rationale is the candidate's own skos:definition and logic:candidateScope, and —
# for the non-entailment ones — the forbidden predicate named by its linked obligation.
# Read over the production ontology (no synthetic data file) this answers "which
# deliberate non-assertions does the ontology guarantee, and of what kind?".
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?candidate ?category WHERE {
    VALUES ?category {
        logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation
        logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap
    }
    ?candidate a logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
               logic:candidateCategory ?category .
}
ORDER BY ?candidate
